      "title": "Set admin audit creation data for entities with an embedded auditable (#5495)",
      "problem_statement": "Set admin audit creation data for entities with an embedded auditable (#5495)\n\n**A Brief Overview**\n7.0.x backport of #3146. `AdminAuditableListener` only set `dateCreated`/`createdBy` on persist when the entity itself implemented `AdminAudit` (a check added in #3106 for BroadleafCommerce/QA#5442), so entities that hold an embedded `AdminAuditable` were saved without creation audit data. The \"already set\" check now also looks at the embedded auditable, so creation data is populated again while existing values are still preserved; covered by a new Spock spec.\n\n**Link to QA issue**\nBroadleafCommerce/QA#5495",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/BroadleafCommerce/BroadleafCommerce/pull/3147",
